<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to auction 3-yr govt. bonds on March 13.</title>
<headline>Hungary to auction 3-yr govt. bonds on March 13.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 25 billion forint worth of the three-year government bonds of 2000/D series on March 13, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest    20 January 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 February 2000</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer	 25,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	 103.18 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction (Feb 13)     104.37 pct</p>
<p>Average yield at last</p>
<p>	 auction		   17.23</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 18.5 percent, payable semi-anually starting from August 12, 1997. -- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
